  "slug": "winter",
  "title": "Winter Color Palettes",
  "tagline": "Deep indigo, ink black, frost white — the quietest register of the Japanese year.",
  "description": "Winter in the Japanese palette is not the white-and-silver of Scandinavian design — it is the layered stillness of ink-on-paper: deep kon indigo, sumi black, cold gofun white, the blue-grey of stone lanterns under frost. Where spring is blush and summer is warmth, winter is restraint taken to its furthest point. These combinations work for premium fashion editorial, high-end architectural identity, technology brands that want authority, and any design that should feel considered and unhurried.",
